            "review_title": "Review at Guangdong Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Markus V\nEspoo, Finland694 contributions\n2\nSmall portions, high price\nOct 2019 • Solo\nI had a quick Dinner in there during ky stay at the hotel.\n\nPlace: it is nice with beautifull view to the sea\n\nService: very kind, but on another hand - i was the only customer 8PM.\n- they need to train English more: i ordered watermelon Juice, got Lemon Juice (and when waitress brang that to the table, she said ”your watermelon...”\n\nWell that was not an issue, i did not complain as lemon Juice is good as well and i’m okay with it.\n\nFood: i had Prawns with chili and Garlic: portion was quite small (4pieces) with no chili flavor and coveres with dried Garlic. It should be a lot bigger and that needs some kind of dip (chili) sauce\n\nBeef: i dont remember the name of the portion. Thin beef steak with Green thing on top of that. Taste was quite OK, but again, small portion.\n\nI had these two meals (see picks), Coke, lemon Juice: 780.000vdn with 5% service fee\n\nI dont eat much, but was still hungry so decided to go to the street and buy Banh Mi.\n\nI have eat chinese Fine dining dozen times around a world and in China - comparing to those this is far behind. As a place in small town in Vietnam - i understand it somehow. \n\nStill - as an experience this was Ok, but value is so low, that i needed to think between two and three stars.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten October 13, 2019",
